# Line endings are pinned only where they affect a shipped artifact.

# build\launcher.bat ships inside the release archive. Without a rule here, git
# rewrites its line endings on checkout according to the per-machine
# core.autocrlf, so two clones of the same commit could pack different bytes
# into the ZIP. CRLF is also what cmd.exe expects from a .bat.
#
# Scoped to *.bat on purpose: nothing else in this repository lands inside an
# artifact, and pinning .ps1 would force a repo-wide reformat for no gain.
*.bat text eol=crlf